{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 10,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Dead flies cause the oil of the perfumer to send forth an evil odor; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doth a little folly outweigh wisdom and honor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wise man’s heart is at his right hand; but a fool’s heart at his left.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yea also, when the fool walketh by the way, his understanding faileth him, and he saith to every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he is a fool.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the spirit of the ruler rise up against thee, leave not thy place; for gentleness allayeth great offences.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, as it were an error which proceedeth from the ruler:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "folly is set in great dignity, and the rich sit in a low place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have seen servants upon horses, and princes walking like servants upon the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that diggeth a pit shall fall into it; and whoso breaketh through a wall, a serpent shall bite him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoso heweth out stones shall be hurt therewith; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that cleaveth wood is endangered thereby.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the iron be blunt, and one do not whet the edge, then must he put to more strength: but wisdom is profitable to direct.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the serpent bite before it is charmed, then is there no advantage in the charmer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The words of a wise man’s mouth are gracious; but the lips of a fool will swallow up himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The beginning of the words of his mouth is foolishness; and the end of his talk is mischievous madness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A fool also multiplieth words: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " man knoweth not what shall be; and that which shall be after him, who can tell him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The labor of fools wearieth every one of them; for he knoweth not how to go to the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to thee, O land, when thy king is a child, and thy princes eat in the morning!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Happy art thou, O land, when thy king is the son of nobles, and thy princes eat in due season, for strength, and not for drunkenness!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By slothfulness the roof sinketh in; and through idleness of the hands the house leaketh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A feast is made for laughter, and wine maketh glad the life; and money answereth all things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ECC.10.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Revile not the king, no, not in thy thought; and revile not the rich in thy bedchamber: for a bird of the heavens shall carry the voice, and that which hath wings shall tell the matter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
